Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:39:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Raise MissingOpError from the loud stubs:
 NotImplementedError + AttributeError

Keras master (3.16-dev) chooses between a backend op and its own
backend-agnostic fallback with `hasattr(backend.ops.numpy, "copysign")`,
`hasattr(backend.ops.math, "lgamma")`, `hasattr(backend.ops.nn,
"rms_normalization")`, ... (#23643 and friends). `hasattr` only swallows
AttributeError, so the PEP 562 stubs' plain NotImplementedError escaped
the probe and would fail even the ops keras can compute without us.

`core.MissingOpError` subclasses both: a direct call stays loud (no
silent fallback, ever), a probe sees absence. The five stub modules raise
it; nothing else changes on keras 3.15.x, where no probe exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C81VdRop6BGDx986cZKWmo
---
 src/keras_tinygrad/_backend/core.py   | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 src/keras_tinygrad/_backend/image.py  |  6 ++++--
 src/keras_tinygrad/_backend/linalg.py |  5 ++++-
 src/keras_tinygrad/_backend/math.py   |  5 ++++-
 src/keras_tinygrad/_backend/nn.py     |  5 ++++-
 src/keras_tinygrad/_backend/numpy.py  |  7 +++++--
 6 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/keras_tinygrad/_backend/core.py b/src/keras_tinygrad/_backend/core.py
index 1f4f76b..1731fb9 100644
--- a/src/keras_tinygrad/_backend/core.py
+++ b/src/keras_tinygrad/_backend/core.py
@@ -19,6 +19,22 @@ from keras.src.backend.common.stateless_scope import StatelessScope
 from keras.src.backend.common.symbolic_scope import SymbolicScope
 
 SUPPORTS_SPARSE_TENSORS = False
+
+
+class MissingOpError(NotImplementedError, AttributeError):
+    """Raised by the backend modules' PEP 562 ``__getattr__`` for an op that
+    is not implemented.
+
+    It IS a ``NotImplementedError``, so a direct call stays loud (no silent
+    fallback, ever). It is ALSO an ``AttributeError``, so ``hasattr(module,
+    name)`` / ``getattr(module, name, default)`` report absence instead of
+    crashing the probe: keras master (3.16-dev) checks
+    ``hasattr(backend.ops.numpy, "copysign")`` and friends before choosing
+    between the backend's op and its own backend-agnostic fallback, and a
+    plain ``NotImplementedError`` escaping that probe would fail even the
+    ops keras could have computed without us.
+    """
+
 SUPPORTS_RAGGED_TENSORS = False
 SUPPORTS_COMPLEX_DTYPES = False
 IS_THREAD_SAFE = True
